 into coherent visual journalism.", "children": [{"id": "25a036a7-c3e8-4351-b7b3-4793e0d1004e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Story development", "children": [{"id": "77c0b9db-cd84-40a9-8135-6f9a7b1176d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Story focus"}, {"id": "173d84e5-652f-4b48-981b-9c38c233cd4d", "type": "concept", "title": "Characters"}, {"id": "c2406091-546d-4456-b031-0fb5a6e398d8", "type": "concept", "title": "Access"}, {"id": "125650ed-708e-4380-9e70-cfe70561f957", "type": "concept", "title": "Reporting plan"}], "description": "Students learn to pitch visual stories with reporting questions, access plans, and ethical considerations."}, {"id": "2681c05a-e700-4aa2-9c6b-ed9972de0b4c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Visual variety", "children": [{"id": "b830b74b-3dd3-4f8a-abd0-fab7be048394", "type": "concept", "title": "Wide shots"}, {"id": "41887d06-bdf2-4b4e-bc63-cfc497d2988c", "type": "concept", "title": "Medium moments"}, {"id": "ae2372e7-97ee-4c59-8d4d-648d726f6eda", "type": "concept", "title": "Details"}, {"id": "99c351c6-42c8-495b-b510-7b6f1927ab6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Portraits"}, {"id": "528fa557-05e8-4c9a-8da9-484d15a38c4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Action"}], "description": "Students build essays with enough range to sustain attention and understanding."}, {"id": "4d624c43-d575-4e08-aa93-fa7ade4f350f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Sequencing and pacing", "children": [{"id": "8525f237-68f3-4a77-9bf8-40898fa900d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Opening image"}, {"id": "69580bf5-1c38-4a20-b6f3-b0f344dc0351", "type": "concept", "title": "Transitions"}, {"id": "bab5866c-4a75-439e-8c99-ed95da9d0637", "type": "concept", "title": "Rhythm"}, {"id": "a25213bc-3abd-4cdb-abc3-0e85b8e2091f", "type": "concept", "title": "Closing image"}], "description": "The goal is to arrange images so the audience experiences discovery, context, tension, and resolution."}]}, {"id": "9f61ecee-2221-4cd0-822d-940fb2fa9115", "type": "topic", "title": "Publishing, Accessibility, and Audience Experience", "description": "Photojournalism reaches audiences through galleries, articles, social platforms, newsletters, print layouts, and mobile screens. Students learn to publish images so they are accessible, contextual, and usable.", "children": [{"id": "172ef44f-6ff0-4430-8518-8f302c9ca29b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform presentation", "children": [{"id": "538e9e55-4109-442c-9d90-5d98f3ddc88a", "type": "concept", "title": "Lead image"}, {"id": "8b261f5d-cfc1-45fa-9d9b-b74d8af6cd6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Gallery edit"}, {"id": "22255b14-17c0-4459-8828-4587e50a7aba", "type": "concept", "title": "Thumbnail"}, {"id": "7e7b282b-cdf6-4233-bf4f-8a50f8c20009", "type": "concept", "title": "Crop variants"}], "description": "Students learn how image choices change across article pages, galleries, social posts, and print."}, {"id": "c3830c0f-8eab-49b0-983a-8afd0849a757", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Accessibility", "children": [{"id": "8b743d6a-f4c9-4b81-8089-7d635fbbbb20", "type": "concept", "title": "Alt text"}, {"id": "60bacdaf-7e0c-4dfc-b64f-8a5f139d4b30", "type": "concept", "title": "Captions vs. alt text"}, {"id": "10e9224c-24ba-4ace-aa9b-de9cf2ed73f3", "type": "concept", "title": "Color contrast"}, {"id": "d3f43c2e-1f7a-431c-b4ee-79a591ef5523", "type": "concept", "title": "Screen-reader context"}], "description": "Students treat accessibility as part of journalistic service and image understanding."}, {"id": "93f69ba4-6291-49c1-9cfc-29671c875655", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audience trust", "children": [{"id": "93acaa63-c64c-4691-9696-b068da89d7fd", "type": "concept", "title": "Headline-image fit"}, {"id": "ca010d10-9727-49a4-b048-c88ecdc7d87f", "type": "concept", "title": "Social framing"}, {"id": "7b9d81d5-dc8d-4131-9374-491574f71445", "type": "concept", "title": "Warnings"}, {"id": "7b5e0a48-53a3-4a05-a0e9-34842bd527f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive context"}], "description": "The point is to avoid decontextualized 